<title>SINGAPORE: Asia Food sees 17 million shares crossed.</title>
<headline>Asia Food sees 17 million shares crossed.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Food &amp; Properties (AFP) saw 17 million shares crossed in early trading on Wednesday, said dealers.</p>
<p>At 0138 GMT, the stock was changing hands at US$1.07, down two cents. Volume was over 19.6 million units.</p>
<p>Dealers said 12 million shares were married at $1 while another five million was done at $1.06.</p>
<p>AFP, controlled by Indonesia's Sinar Mas Tunggal, has interests in property and food distribution mainly in Indonesia.  </p>
<p>Dealers said HSBC James Capel had called for a buy on AFP up to $1 and brought the company on a roadshow.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
